<title>HONG KONG: HK August retail sales up 5.0 pct in value on yr.</title>
<headline>HK August retail sales up 5.0 pct in value on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong August retail sales totalled a provisional HK$19.1 billion, up five percent on the year and up one percent on the month, Census and Statistics Department figures showed.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value and volume of all retail outlets</p>
<p>						     August  July</p>
<p> Total retail sales (on-year)  - value   +5	+7</p>
<p>					 - volume  +1.5    +3</p>
<p>			  (on-month) - value   +1	+8</p>
<p>					 - volume  +1	+9</p>
<p>Breakdown by category (on-year)</p>
<p> Clothing and footwear	   - value   +9	+5</p>
<p>					 - volume  +1	-1</p>
<p>Jewellery, watches</p>
<p> clocks, valuable gifts	  - value   +4	+5</p>
<p>					 - volume  +2	+4</p>
<p>Consumer durables,</p>
<p> excluding cars		    - value   +9	+10</p>
<p>					 - volume  +8	+9</p>
<p> Department stores		 - value   +5	+2</p>
<p>					 - volume  +1	-3</p>
<p> Supermarkets			- value   +5	 +7</p>
<p>					 - volume  -1	 +1</p>
<p> Fuels				 - value   -13	-9</p>
<p>					 - volume  -18     -16</p>
<p> Motor vehicles		    - value    +8     +34</p>
<p>					 - volume   +7     +32</p>
<p>Food, alcoholic drinks and</p>
<p> tobacco			     - value    -8	+5</p>
<p>					 - volume   -6	**</p>
<p>** = virtually unchanged</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
